      "parent_msg_id": ""
    },
    {
      "to": "BASTION",
      "cc": ["RAMPART", "PLUMBLINE", "ARCHON"],
      "type": "INS",
      "priority": "high",
      "subject": "Site Directive: Piling Hold on Array Block 6 & Implementation of FDC-CIV-001",
      "body": "Site operational directive for EVT-001: Enforce an immediate HOLD on all direct hydraulic ramming in Array Block 6 due to rock refusal encountered at 0.8m depth against the 1.5m tender design assumption. Driving piles against hard rock without pre-drilling is prohibited to prevent pile shaft buckling. Field Design Change FDC-CIV-001 is issued requiring DTH pre-drilling and annular grouting. Piling rigs shall be re-sequenced to non-rock array blocks to maintain progress on WP-CON-CIV-PIL (scope 15,400 piles, delivered 0.0, installed 0.0, QC accepted 0.0, IFC False). Production piling in Block 6 shall not commence until pre-drilling trial piles are installed, tested, and certified by PLUMBLINE.",
      "action_by_day": 6,
      "parent_msg_id": ""
    },
    {
      "to": "MERIDIAN",
      "cc": ["ARCHON", "PLUMBLINE"],
      "type": "RFI",
      "priority": "high",
      "subject": "Urgent Geotechnical Data Request: Block 6 Rock Strata Delineation & Mechanical Properties",
      "body": "Following EVT-001 rock refusal at 0.8m depth in Array Block 6, TERRA requires certified geotechnical investigation data to finalize pile design calculations (HEL-ST-CAL-0010) and support FDC-CIV-001. Per TERRA authority limits, no civil IFC will be issued without certified geotechnical data. Please execute confirmatory boreholes on a staggered grid in Block 6 to map the rock interface, and provide laboratory test results including Unconfined Compressive Strength (UCS per GOST 21153.2-84 / ASTM D7012), Rock Quality Designation (RQD %), and chemical analysis for groundwater/soil sulfate aggressiveness to confirm annular grout mix design.",
